Two build failures players reported: a Vulkan SDK on the machine, and a space
in the folder path.

1. runtime.cmake: PSX_ENABLE_VULKAN defaulted ON, so on a machine with the
   Vulkan SDK installed ($VULKAN_SDK, glslc) the configure added a custom step
   that runs ${PSXRECOMP_ROOT}/tools/embed_spirv.py. The framework payload this
   port ships carries no tools/ directory, so ninja stopped with "missing and
   no known rule to make it" on every build. Crash 2 Recompiled offers OpenGL
   and Direct3D 12 only, so the option now defaults OFF, and even when ON (a
   cache from an earlier configure, or -D on the command line) the backend
   falls back to its software stub when embed_spirv.py is not in the tree.

2. main_cli.cpp: run_process started psxrecomp-game and psxrecomp-bios with
   _spawnv, which joins argv with single spaces and quotes nothing. The child's
   C runtime split any argument holding a space again, so a game unpacked into
   "D:\Crash Bandicoot 2" failed at "[3/4] Recompiling BIOS" with "config file
   not found: D:\Crash". Every argument is now quoted the way the C runtime
   parses it back (backslashes literal except before a quote). The launcher
   ships a CLI built from this tree (_build/build_recompiler.ps1 builds it in
   _build/build-cli with PSXRECOMP_ENABLE_CHD=ON so .chd discs still read)
   instead of the stock one.

main_cli.cpp is not in codegen_hash_sources.cmake and runtime.cmake does not
change generated code; the codegen hash is unchanged (3d2b5a19).

